Skia: silence deprecated XML_SetHashSalt under SDK pkg expat.

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), not submitted upstream.
Source: Chromium electron-source tree under EmberBSD.
Apply after other third_party/skia patches.
NetBSD SDK pkg expat deprecates XML_SetHashSalt in favor of
XML_SetHashSalt16Bytes; keep the legacy salt call (Skia has not switched)
and wrap it so -Wdeprecated-declarations does not fail under -Werror.

--- a/third_party/skia/src/xml/SkXMLParser.cpp
+++ b/third_party/skia/src/xml/SkXMLParser.cpp
@@ -175,7 +175,12 @@
     // random salt once per process oursevles ensures the salt is non-deterministic
     // and unguessable, while preventing calls to rand_s inside sandboxed processes
     // on Windows.
+#pragma clang diagnostic push
+#pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Wdeprecated-declarations"
+    // SDK expat deprecates XML_SetHashSalt in favor of XML_SetHashSalt16Bytes;
+    // keep legacy salt until Skia switches (Werror on NetBSD pkg expat).
     XML_SetHashSalt(ctx.fXMLParser, get_hash_salt());
+#pragma clang diagnostic pop
 
     XML_SetUserData(ctx.fXMLParser, &ctx);
     XML_SetElementHandler(ctx.fXMLParser, start_element_handler, end_element_handler);
